              "message": "=You are a smart assistant that extracts structured answers from conversations with potential home buyers. Your task is to read through the conversation or text and extract the answers to five screening questions used to qualify them.\n\nFocus on returning only the buyer’s answers, not the questions themselves. Be concise, use natural phrasing, and ensure no important context is lost.\n\nThe five questions you must extract answers to are:\n\n1. **Budget**: What’s their budget range for purchasing a property?\n2. **Timeline**: Are they buying soon, or still exploring?\n3. **Mortgage**: Do they have a mortgage agreement in principle, or do they need help?\n4. **Property Type**: What kind of property are they looking for (e.g. detached, semi-detached, flat)?\n5. **Preferred Areas**: Which areas or neighbourhoods are they most interested in?\n\nReturn the output as a JSON object like this:\n{\n  \"budgetRange\": \"Around £350,000 to £400,000\",\n  \"timeline\": \"Looking to buy within the next 3 months\",\n  \"mortgageStatus\": \"No mortgage yet — open to help arranging one\",\n  \"propertyType\": \"Prefer a semi-detached house with 3 bedrooms\",\n  \"preferredAreas\": \"Headington, Cowley, or central Oxford\"\n}"
            }
          ]
